# Sidecar binaries directory: track placeholder stubs, ignore real PyInstaller artefacts.
# Real binaries are large PyInstaller bundles — they are replaced during the release
# workflow and must never be committed.  The placeholder stubs (shell scripts) are
# committed so that `cargo check` succeeds on every platform without a real build.
#
# Convention: a real binary is larger than 1 MB; a placeholder stub is a few bytes.
# We rely on build tooling (see CI workflow) to overwrite the stub before bundling.


